          },
          "mechanism": "Hypertension diagnosis is the clinical condition triggering antihypertensive medication prescription, placing it in the causal pathway to the outcome. Acetaminophen use might causally affect blood pressure through chronic inflammation or direct pharmacologic effects, making hypertension a potential mediator. Alternatively, if acetaminophen does not causally affect hypertension development, the diagnosis is purely a confounder.",
          "justification": "The causal direction between acetaminophen use and hypertension development is unknown from the literature and the data. This variable is either a confounder (if association is due to common causes) or a mediator (if acetaminophen affects blood pressure).",
          "role": "confounder_or_mediator",
          "proxy_for": null,
          "contestable": false
        }
      ],
